{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_150","type":"agent_message","text":"I have ample material. Let me write the comprehensive update handoff now.\n\n---\n\n# REVIEW ROUND 1 — UPDATED RESEARCH HANDOFF\n\n**Job:** `dossier:2023-population-top20-canonical-full-v1:2023:MEX:15802`\n**Ruler:** Andrés Manuel López Obrador (AMLO), President of Mexico 2018–2024\n**Period:** 2023 calendar year\n**Worker:** internet-research subagent, review round 1\n**Sandbox note:** local-write still blocked by `bwrap: loopback: Failed RTM_NEWADDR`. Both `research-materials.md` and `research-ledger-manifest.json` to be persisted by parent agent using the contents below. Files were last cycle's deliverables; this round updates them per reviewer brief.\n\nThis handoff (a) corrects the 14 reviewer findings, (b) replaces snippet-only claims with primary locators, (c) splits bundled claims into distinct stable IDs with many-to-many lens mappings, (d) drops researcher-written score anchors and judging recommendations, and (e) records chapter saturation and remaining gaps explicitly.\n\n---\n\n## A. Reviewer-finding response matrix\n\n| Reviewer issue | Status | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2B-E02 bundles Mérida + migration cooperation | addressed | split into `2B-E02A` (Mérida discontinuation) and `2B-E02B` (Biden Title-8 cooperation) |\n| 2B lacks primary attribution | partial | added `2B-E04` direct EO executive-order citation (visa ban decree) and `2B-E07` direct AMLO quote from Forbes on Cuba/Nicaragua/Venezuela |\n| 3B-E01/E02 are snippet-only | addressed | replaced with `3B-E04` (Animal Político/AFP Hurricane Otis reporting), `3B-E05` (France 24) and `3B-E06` (UN OCHA SitRep) with precise locators |\n| 3B lacks crisis-response evidence | addressed | added `3B-E04`–`3B-E08` Hurricane Otis (Oct 25, 2023) with primary documentation |\n| 4B Pegasus lacks registered source | addressed | added `4B-E11` (Animal Político/R3D primary article, 7 March 2023) with locator |\n| 4B women/minorities evidence thin | partial | added `4B-E12` (Freedom House FoN 2024, A5/B5 disinformation against Piña) |\n| 5B Inter-American Dialogue claims bundled | addressed | split into `5B-E02A`–`5B-E02F` (each author/lens separately) |\n| 5B 2024 budget comparison not target period | addressed | dropped and replaced with `5B-E03A` (INEGI 2023 GDP 3.2%) and `5B-E03B` (INEGI 2023 GDP sectors) and `5B-E03C` (CONASAMI minimum-wage primary) |\n| 5B lacks primary welfare outcomes | partial | added `5B-E06` (CONASAMI minimum-wage 20%) and `5B-E07` (García-Ponce/GWU academic) |\n| 6B-E01 duplicates 5B | addressed | removed; folded into shared `5B-E02A`; 6B now has only welfare-specific items |\n| 6B pandemic-mismanagement snippet | addressed | removed as standalone; folded into `6B-E07` (Wikipedia/UN OCHA Otis) which captures the catastrophic 2023 crisis-response pattern |\n| 7B trust-fund bundled | addressed | split into `7B-E03A` (FAMI 135.9 B pesos), `7B-E03B` (2,300% increase), `7B-E03C` (no new controls), `7B-E03D` (109 trust funds eliminated), `7B-E03E` (44 B peso 2020 audit discrepancy) |\n| 7B family business unresolved | addressed | added `7B-E12` (AQ \"Forever Agenda\" reference to family graft allegations) with caveat |\n| 8B 2024 outcomes confused with 2023 | addressed | separated `8B-E07` (Maya Train Sept 2023 handover) and `8B-E08` (Tulum airport + customs to Sedena Sept 2023) |\n| Researcher-written score ranges | addressed | all removed; this handoff records only source-claim units and lens mappings |\n\n---\n\n## B. Stable global evidence ledger (post-review)\n\nEach item is a distinct materially different claim with one source and one locator. IDs are stable across chapters and reused for many-to-many lens mappings. Where an item appeared in the previous round, the *same* provisional ID is preserved.\n\n### Primary external evidence (post-review)\n\n| ID | Canonical fact key | Claim summary | URL / locator | Disposition | Chapters / lenses |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n