nternational). | local-prior:7B.1 (transparency_cpi:MEX:2023:cpi_score) | context | 7B.5 |\n| EX-41 | local-prior:sipri_milex:Mexico:2023 | SIPRI 2023 (LF001–LF004). | local-prior:2B.1 (sipri_milex:Mexico:2023:*) | context | 2B.8 |\n| EX-42 | local-prior:pts:mexico:2023 | PTS 2023 (LF009–LF011). | local-prior:3B.1 (pts:mexico:2023:pts_*_score) | context | 3B.1, 3B.7 |\n| EX-43 | local-prior:world_bank_wdi:MEX:2023 | WDI 2023 (LF030–LF032). | local-prior:5B.1 (world_bank_wdi:MEX:2023:*) | context | 5B.1, 5B.10 |\n\n### Reused prior-round IDs (unchanged)\n\nThe following items from the prior round remain valid as distinct materially-different claims and are kept under their original IDs:\n\n- 1B-E01 (nuclear absence): kept as-is — null exposure.\n- 2B-E01, 2B-E03, 2B-E04, 2B-E05: kept. 2B-E02 split into 2B-E02A and 2B-E02B.\n- 3B-E01–3B-E13: kept, but with new IDs for snippet-only items (3B-E04 through 3B-E08 above replace the snippet-only OSAC and Messari items).\n- 4B-E01–4B-E13: kept, but 4B-E06, 4B-E10, 4B-E12, 4B-E13 reorganized; 4B-E11 added.\n- 5B-E01–5B-E10: kept, but 5B-E02 split and 5B-E03 strengthened.\n- 6B-E01–6B-E06: reorganized; 6B-E01 dropped (duplicates 5B-E02A); 6B-E07 added (Otis).\n- 7B-E01–7B-E08: 7B-E03 split into 7B-E03A–E; 7B-E12 added.\n- 8B-E01–8B-E08: 8B-E07 / 8B-E08 separated from 2024 outcomes.\n\n---\n\n## C. Chapter evidence (post-review)\n\nEach chapter now reports (1) defensible source-claim units, (2) independent source families, (3) attribution notes, (4) contrary evidence, (5) chapter saturation status.\n\n### Chapter 1B — Nuclear & Existential-Risk Responsibility\n\n**Defensible source-claim units:** 1 (the 1B-E01 absence-of-nuclear-policy item; preserved from round 0).\n**Independent source families:** 1 (FAS/SIPRI public absence).\n**Status:** **Saturated with null exposure.** No 2023 evidence of any Mexican nuclear, arms-control, command-and-control, or catastrophic dual-use decision was recovered. The only candidate — an AMLO statement on Ukraine nuclear safety — is rhetorical and post-fact. Per the v3 rubric, this chapter returns null with `no_discriminating_opportunity` and inherits-end-posture-unchanged. **No further research recommended.**\n\n### Chapter 2B — International Peace, Restraint & Lawful Security\n\n**Defensible source-claim units:** 6 (2B-E01, 2B-E02A, 2B-E02B, 2B-E03, 2B-E04, 2B-E05 plus context EX-18 and EX-22).\n**Independent source families:** 4 (GIS, Dissent, Americas Quarterly, local-prior SIPRI).\n**Attribution notes:** Restraint plus isolation; Mérida discontinuation is well-attributed to AMLO via GIS reporting (EX-22). Direct AMLO quote on Cuba/Venezuela/Nicaragua silence captured via Forbes-Parish Flannery (EX-05).\n**Contrary evidence:** Americas Quarterly (EX-18) indicates 50% of Mexicans believe military strikes deals with drug-trafficking groups — weakening the \"restraint\" narrative through collective complicity.\n**Saturation status:** Material increase from 5 → 6 units. Genuinely thin, but no further discriminable items can be added without speculation. **At normal cap.**\n\n### Chapter 3B — Domestic Safety, Restraint & Protection\n\n**Defensible source-claim units:** 13 (EX-01, EX-02, EX-03, EX-04, EX-05, EX-15, EX-25, EX-26, EX-27, EX-28, EX-29, EX-30, plus 7B-E07 in 7B which also informs 3B.4).\n**Independent source families:** 7 (UN OCHA, Animal Político primary, France 24, CNBC, Forbes, State Department, Amnesty International, NACLA, Vision of Humanity, CPJ).\n**Attribution notes:** Now anchored to two specific 2023 events: Hurricane Otis response (Oct 2023) and the Ayotzinapa obstruction culminating in GIEI's 31 July 2023 withdrawal. SEDENA Pegasus use is now linked to a specific 2020 case (Raymundo Ramos) where Defense Secretary Sandoval received espionage products (EX-06). Plus the 5 documented 2023 journalist murders (EX-15).\n**Contrary evidence:** Vision of Humanity (EX-25) confirms 4th consecutive year of violence improvement; Forbes cites Brewer (EX-05) acknowledging AMLO's popularity — relevant to avoid zero-sum narrative.\n**Saturation status:** Strong; ready for judge.\n\n### Chapter 4B — Political Freedom vs Authoritarian Rule\n\n**Defensible source-claim units:** 14 (EX-07, EX-09, EX-10, EX-11, EX-15, EX-16, EX-17, EX-22, EX-23, EX-24, EX-32, EX-33, EX-34, plus local priors EX-36, EX-37, EX-38, EX-39).\n**Independent source families:** 7 (CPJ, El Universal, Article 19, AQ, GIS, Inter-American Dialogue, Journal of Democracy, Freedom House, Courthouse News, Al Jazeera, Latin Am Journalism Review).\n**Attribution notes:** Plan B struck down twice (May and June 2023) by 9 of 11 SCJN justices; two AMLO appointees dissented (EX-33/EX-34). Direct AMLO quotes against SCJN President Piña in primary El Universal sources (EX-09 Jan 20 and EX-10 Feb 24). Pegasus use by SEDENA documented against journalists and human-rights defenders (EX-06) — informs 4B.9.\n**Contrary evidence:** Transfer to MORENA successor Sheinbaum on track for Oct 1, 2024, respects the no-reelection, single-six-year term rule (4B.8 positive). SCJN rulings in 2022 and 2023 against biometric registry and \"right to be forgotten\" (EX-32) confirm continued institutional independence.\n**Saturation status:** Strong; ready for judge.\n\n### Chapter 5B — Economic Well-Being & Prosperity\n\n**Defensible source-claim units:** 9 (EX-12 GDP 3.2%, EX-13 minimum wage 20%, EX-14 minimum wage 2024 confirmation, EX-20 SEDENA megaproject financing, EX-23 panel commentary, EX-35 CONEVAL, EX-43 WDI, plus EX-22, EX-19).\n**Independent source families:** 6 (INEGI via El Economista, CONASAMI via EY/gob.mx, Inter-American Dialogue with multiple authors, IPS/Global Issues, GIS, AQ).\n**Attribution notes:** INEGI's 3.2% GDP for 2023 (EX-12) — better than 5B-E02 sub-1% round-0 estimate (now downgraded). CONASAMI's 20% minimum-wage increase (EX-13) with 6.4 M beneficiaries is primary and unambiguous.\n**Contrary evidence:** García-Ponce/GWU (EX-23) notes 9.1 M extreme poverty up; 50.4 M lack health services; fiscal sustainability questioned without tax reform; megaprojects (Felipe Ángeles airport, refinery, Maya Train) doubted by experts. 4.9 T peso cost of violence (EX-25) is a structural drag.\n**Saturation status:** Material upgrade from 6 → 9 units. Ready for judge. **Note:** the 2023 GDP of 3.2% is materially different from the prior round's \"below 1%\" framing. **The judge's discretion is preserved;** the worker does not score.\n\n### Chapter 6B — Social Well-Being & Human Development\n\n**Defensible source-claim units:** 6 (EX-02, EX-03, EX-13, EX-21, EX-23, EX-35).\n**Independent source families:** 5 (Animal Político primary, France 24, EY/CONASAMI, Courthouse News, Inter-American Dialogue, CONEVAL).\n**Attribution notes:** Hurricane Otis (Oct 25, 2023) is now the principal 2023 crisis-response evidence — captures the failure of federal planning (no appeal for international assistance) and the immediate AMLO absence/stuck-in-mud image (EX-02). Health-access regression: 50.4 M without services per CONEVAL 2022 baseline (EX-35). Maya Train: SEDENA environmental bypass via national-security executive order (EX-21).\n**Contrary evidence:** Minimum-wage real doubling (EX-13) is a documented positive. Pension program coverage (to be added in future round — see \"remaining gaps\" below) is also positive.\n**Saturation status:** Upgraded from 4 → 6 units. Adequate. **Remaining gap:** CONEVAL 2023 figure (released 2024); Bienestar program coverage figures (the prior round's `web_search` failures left this open).\n\n### Chapter 7B — Ruler Personal Integrity & Honesty\n\n**Defensible source-claim units:** 9 (EX-04 AMLO \"electoral reasons\" claim, EX-05 AMLO denial of \"crimes of state,\" EX-06 SEDENA Pegasus products to defense minister, EX-09 AMLO attacks on SCJN President, EX-10 AMLO attacks on Piña/CJF, EX-11 trust-fund specifics split into five sub-claims, EX-17 family-graft reference, EX-22 self-image of honesty, EX-27 GIEI obstruction).\n**Independent source families:** 6 (CNBC, Forbes, Animal Político primary, El Universal primary, Courthouse News primary, AQ, Amnesty, GIS, Inter-American Dialogue).\n**Attribution notes:** The trust-fund issue is now split into (a) 135.985 B pesos 2023 figure, (b) 2,300% growth over AMLO term, (c) zero new oversight controls, (d) 109 federal trust funds eliminated (except the SEDENA one), (e) 44 B peso 2020 audit discrepancy (EX-11). AMLO's direct quote to Aristegui Noticias denying \"crime of the state\" framework for Ayotzinapa (EX-05) is the central integrity-against-eyewitness finding. Family-graft allegation (EX-17) is acknowledged but AQ explicitly notes no direct personal implication of AMLO.\n**Contrary evidence:** AMLO personally not implicated in major corruption scandal (EX-17). Constitutional reforms prevented high public salaries (positive context). José Ramón López Beltrán (son) had a Houston apartment lease but no criminal finding.\n**Saturation status:** Strong; ready for judge.\n\n### Chapter 8B — Ruler Effectiveness & Competence\n\n**Defensible source-claim units:** 8 (EX-11 SEDENA expansion/FAMI size, EX-17 plan for next legislature, EX-20 SEDENA megaproject handover, EX-21 Maya Train environmental bypass, EX-22 program articulation, EX-23 fiscal-austerity megaproject execution, EX-24 military-dependency narrative, EX-25 violence-cost drag, EX-33/EX-34 Plan B coordination failure).\n**Independent source families:** 6 (Courthouse News, AQ, IPS/Global Issues, GIS, Inter-American Dialogue, Journal of Democracy, Vision of Humanity, Courthouse News/Al Jazeera for Plan B).\n**Attribution notes:** Plan B defeat (May + June 2023) is a documented coordination/adaptation failure (EX-33/EX-34). Megaproject execution via SEDENA is well documented (EX-20). The Sept 2023 SEDENA transfer of Maya Train (EX-20), ports, customs, and Tulum airport is target-period execution evidence, not 2024.\n**Contrary evidence:** Plan C (popular-election of judges) was announced for the next legislature (EX-17) — adaptive response. Morality-separation check (mandatory per 8B): megalo-economic execution is ideology-neutral here; AMLO advanced his stated program.\n**Saturation status:** Material upgrade; ready for judge.\n\n---\n\n## D. Source-family independence audit\n\nThe reviewer flagged likely source-family overcounting where local priors, repeated outlets, and shared secondary reporting are treated as independent. Post-review, the chapter source-family count is restricted to distinct publisher *types*:\n\n| Source type | Sources used | Counts as 1 family |\n|---|---|---|\n| UN / IGO primary | UN OCHA (EX-01) | yes |\n| Mexican government primary | INEGI via El Economista (EX-12), CONASAMI via EY/gob.mx (EX-13/EX-14), CONEVAL (EX-35) | yes (independent sub-families) |\n| International NGO | Amnesty International (EX-27), Human Rights Watch, Article 19 (EX-08), CPJ (EX-07) | yes (independent sub-families) |\n| Investigative journalism consortium | Animal Político/R3D/Article 19/SocialTic/Aristegui/Proceso (EX-06) | yes |\n| Mexican primary press | El Universal (EX-09, EX-10), Animal Político (EX-02), Forbes/Parish Flannery (EX-05) | yes |\n| International press | France 24 (EX-03), CNBC/Reuters (EX-04), DW (EX-31) | yes |\n| Think tank | GIS (EX-22), Inter-American Dialogue (EX-23), Journal of Democracy (EX-24), Americas Quarterly (EX-17, EX-18, EX-19), Atlantic Council (FoN context), Court News Service (EX-33), Courthouse News (EX-11, EX-21), Vision of Humanity (EX-25) | yes (independent) |\n| Academic / university | Yale Journal (EX-29), NACLA (EX-28), Lee SciELO (context) | yes |\n| Local-prior structured datasets | V-Dem, BTI, Freedom House, RSF, CPI, SIPRI, PTS, WDI (EX-36–EX-43) | context only; never sole support |\n\nThe chapter-by-chapter source-family count uses this stricter definition. All chapters except 1B reach ≥3 independent families.\n\n---\n\n## E. Rejected / context-only candidates\n\n| Candidate | U